== "full":` to `if normalized == "full" or "full" in normalized.split(","):`\n  
- Line 324: Changed `if normalized == "full":` to `if normalized == "full" or 
"full" in normalized.split(","):`\n\n## Test Files Created\n1. 
`tests/agents/test_working_memory_full_token_bug.py` - Contains 6 tests that 
demonstrate the bug and verify the fix\n2. 
`tests/agents/test_working_memory_full_contains_bug.py` - Additional tests for 
the bug\n\n## Verification\n- All existing tests pass (111 tests in 
working_memory test suite)\n- New bug-specific tests pass\n- The fix correctly 
handles:\n  - `"full,10-20"` → file considered fully read\n  - `"10-20,full"` → 
file considered fully read  \n  - `"full , 10-20"` (with spaces) → file 
considered fully read\n  - `"FULL,10-20"` (uppercase) → file considered fully 
read\n  - `"full"` (exact) → still works\n  - `"  full  "` (with spaces) → still
works'})
